<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry III the White</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1227–<a href="/years/1266">1266</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry III the White was a Silesian Piast duke, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-the-pious">Henry II the Pious</a>, who received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wroclaw">Wrocław</a> when his father's duchy was divided in 1248. He ruled Wrocław from 1248 to 1266, at first jointly with his brother Władysław, and encouraged German settlement and the town's recovery after the Mongol invasion of 1241. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-probus">Henry IV Probus</a> succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-iii-the-white.jpg" alt="Henry III the White" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henryk_III_Bia%C5%82y_seal.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
